.TH EBC 1 "2026-07-28" "ebasic 0.1.0" "eBasic Manual"
.SH NAME
ebc \- the eBasic compiler
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ebc
.I input.bas
.RB [ \-o
.IR output ]
.RB [ \-cxx
.IR compiler ]
.RB [ \-L
.IR dir ]...
.RB [ \-I
.IR dir ]...
.RB [ \-l
.IR name ]...
.RB [ \-\-keep\-cpp ]
.RB [ \-\-lib ]
.br
.B ebc
.RB { \-v | \-\-version }
.br
.B ebc
.RB { \-h | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ebc
transpiles \fIinput.bas\fR (eBasic source) to C++ and invokes a real
backend compiler (g++ or clang++) to produce a native executable, or,
with \fB\-\-lib\fR, a static library.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-o " output"
Output path. Defaults to the input file's own stem.
.TP
.BI \-cxx " compiler"
Backend compiler to invoke. Defaults to the
.B CXX
environment variable if set, else the bare name
.BR g++ .
.TP
.BI \-L " dir"
Extra library search path, forwarded to the backend as \fB\-L\fR \fIdir\fR. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-I " dir"
Extra #include search path for .bas source, consulted only as a fallback.
Repeatable.
.TP
.BI \-l " name"
Extra library to link. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-cpp
Don't delete the generated \fI<output>.gen.cpp\fR intermediate file.
.TP
.B \-\-lib
Build a library (a static archive plus an auto-generated interface file)
instead of an executable.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ebpm (1),
.BR docgen (1)
.br
Full documentation: <https://github.com/yann64/ebasic/blob/main/docs/guide/ebc.md>
